==============================================================================
FINAL THEOREM (K=3, PROVED)
==============================================================================
For all n>=6 and all x in [0,1]:
  |Delta_n(x)| = |F_n^(3)(x) - F_3(x)| <= C3/n,
  C3 = 0.718333582186124000803872773285
     (0.8794% above the pure asymptotic-leading constant M3_exact = 0.712071558138028)
  vs. the crude constant 22 on record (Corollary D3.5) -- a 30.63x tightening.

Boundary values n=3,4,5 (outside this theorem's n>=6 domain, same domain restriction as the archive's own crude Corollary D3.5):
  n=3: exact sup_x|Delta_n(x)| = |Delta_3(1)| = 1  (trivially <= 22/3 = 22/3)
  n=4: exact sup_x|Delta_n(x)| = |Delta_4(1)| = 1/4  (trivially <= 22/4 = 11/2)
  n=5: exact sup_x|Delta_n(x)| = |Delta_5(1)| = 1/10  (trivially <= 22/5 = 22/5)
